    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263">

                <pb facs="0463" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296A/45</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Basel</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cochran</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Basel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-23">November 23, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received December
                        4.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith five
                    copies of a press communiqué, dated November 20, 1931,<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d263-f1"/> in which the B. I. S. announced the steps that it had
                    taken, following the receipt of the German request for the convocation of the
                    Special Advisory Committee.</p>
                <p>There are also attached five copies each of the English translations, made in the
                    B. I. S., of the note under which the Memorandum was transmitted, and of the
                    Memorandum itself, the official text whereof was in German.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Merle Cochran</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d263-a1.xml" xpointer="d263-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d263-a2.xml" xpointer="d263-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
